    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-1986-p14.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The quotient \\(\\dfrac{b}{a}\\) is largest with the biggest \\(b\\) and smallest \\(a,\\) giving \\(\\dfrac{1200}{200} = 6.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is C .",
      "hints": [
        "A quotient is largest when the numerator is as large as possible and the denominator as small as possible",
        "Use the largest \\(b\\) and the smallest \\(a\\)"
